// Title: Renamed PsExec Service Execution
// Sigma ID: 51ae86a2-e2e1-4097-ad85-c46cb6851de4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects suspicious launch of a renamed version of the PSEXESVC service with, which is not often
//   used by legitimate administrators
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative tasks
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/psexec
//   - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ro2QuZTIMBM
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_sysinternals_psexec_service.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "psexesvc.exe" and (not(FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\PSEXESVC.exe"))
